**Rule (Private Accounting inventory)** · `rule:nrz:cas-backend-registration`

Accounting's actual backing is the vector row above; its `bytes` remains the enforcing logical judgment-plus-registration allowance, not that measurement. Namespace Arc identity prevents a dropped store from aliasing a later store. Same-store refresh changes the reserved amount after existing charged visits, without a second entry or graph-payload allocation. Registration growth via `try_reserve_exact`, forget's removal/boxed-slice replacement, and restore's optional push have distinct allocation transitions. Include old/new coexistence and any restoration backing. Snapshot/restore affects only that store; other registrations survive. Forgetting one store does not prove the vector's remaining capacity was released.

The namespace control allocation outlives Cas if any registration still holds its strong Arc. While the store lives, the fixed-store owner row attributes that allocation once; on store destruction attribution transfers to the surviving registration owners, without treating the move as release or a new allocation. Several ledgers still share that same identity, and the last strong edge releases it. Keep this control allocation as an explicit child of the surviving registration inventory. The per-entry 64-byte logical metadata allowance is not a supported physical-capacity bound for this control allocation or the vector backing; do not claim that it covers either in a complete physical inventory. Its existing enforcing value stays unchanged. The referenced initial-allocation figure is `STORE = size_of(Cas)+384` in (`req:nrz:lc-graph-cas-backend-prerequisite`), the bundled inline-store/two-initial-allocation allowance; it is not a separately measured namespace-control size. The consumer's existing STORE enforcing row and the CAS-local attribution of the namespace control allocation are separate projections. Attribution follows the last registration edge even after store destruction; it does not split, prolong or revise the existing consumer STORE debit. F's new complete-aggregate inventory must keep that surviving allocation visible under its own justified projection until actual release, with the shared-allocation intersection explicit.

Distinguish registration slots, namespace edges, committed `Cas::retained_judgment_bytes()` and unpublished pending payload. Deduplicate physical attribution without removing the persistent enforcing reservation on later calls. Accounting Work tariffs are outside the retained-map scope stated at the head of (`sec:nrz:cas-backend-inventory`); its existing charging behavior remains. Restoration must remain possible after exhaustion: retain or preprepare the necessary backing before a fallible attempt rather than depend on a new unpaid operation. These facts require CAS-local controls because Accounting is pub(crate); matrix cannot inspect its private capacity.

**Rule (Logical and backend overlap)** · `rule:nrz:cas-backend-overlap`

Logical payload/proof reservations and native capacity are separate projections with an explicit allocation intersection. Inline Vertex slots are already in graph node capacity; adding a whole logical vertex tariff as another physical allocation would double count. Replace an aggregate with justified disjoint child projections, or keep the aggregate and add only demonstrated uncovered allocations; never subtract an enforcing reservation merely to make a report smaller. A logical key or graph allowance alone is not an observed backing.

Apply this partition to B_corr and `C_x+A_x−S_x` under (`rule:nrz:descriptor-binding-lc-omega-resources`). STORE/C0, the frozen carrier/control, law payload and original baseline U already have owners. Backend growth is their uncovered increment, not another complete Cas or another law. Shared law/key/certificate/environment identities count once; independently allocated equal buffers and certificate copies remain distinct. `retained_judgment_bytes` belongs to graph logical payload and may also be enforced through Accounting; this is one physical payload with multiple enforcing scopes, not two payloads. Registration backing and inline edges are separate. Preserve the simultaneous phase union and final-owner release under (`rule:nrz:lc-graph-retained-overlap`), including refusal, freeze, sharing and refresh.

